<title>GREECE: NATL MORTGAGE BANK SETS INTEREST RATES ON ITS BONDS.</title>
<headline>NATL MORTGAGE BANK SETS INTEREST RATES ON ITS BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>State National Mortgage Bank of Greece said in a statement that its bonds that expire on August 31 and have not completed five years will be renewed for one year at 15 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds issued in August 1996 will carry a pre-tax rate of 15 percent, it said. -- Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
